	(text "Pin 1 = OUTx, pin 2 = that load's ground return (DEC-013, decided 2026-10-22).\nLAYOUT: each pin 2 return carries up to 10 A, like its OUTx: same copper and via treatment.\n  Route pin 2 returns to the power-entry ground star region, never across the logic ground.\n  Up to 60 A of load return flows from the headers to the star region and out through J902.\nRELEASE-BLOCKING: which physical hole is pin 1 (TE drawing vs application spec): check a real part."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
